        {
            "source_entity_instance": "gas chromatograph (GC) (7890A)",
            "source_entity_type": "Instrument",
            "relation": "MEASURES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "AM fungal biomass",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "AM fungal biomass in soil was measured using the phospholipid fatty acid (PLFA) method77. Briefly, freeze-dried soil samples (5.0 g) were weighed to extract total lipids in a chloroform-methanol-citrate buffer (1: 2: 0.8, v/v/v) after shaking for 1 h. The extracted lipids were fractionated into neutral, glyco- and phospholipids on a silicic-acid column by eluting chloroform, acetone, and methanol, respectively. The separated fatty-acid methyl esters were analyzed by a gas chromatograph (GC) (7890A, Agilent Technologies, Santa Clara, CA, USA) coupled with a MIDI peak-identification system (MIDI, Inc. Newark, DE, USA).",
